            "output": " std::from\\_chars - cppreference.com             \n\n##### [cppreference.com](/)\n\n##### Search\n\n  🔍\n\n[Create account](/index.php?title=Special:CreateAccount&returnto=cpp%2Futility%2Ffrom+chars \"You are encouraged to create an account and log in; however, it is not mandatory\")\n\n-   [Log in](/index.php?title=Special:UserLogin&returnto=cpp%2Futility%2Ffrom+chars \"You are encouraged to log in; however, it is not mandatory [o]\")\n\n##### Namespaces\n\n-   [Page](/cpp/utility/from_chars \"View the content page [c]\")\n-   [Discussion](/Talk:cpp/utility/from_chars \"Discussion about the content page [t]\")\n\n##### Variants[](#)\n\n##### Views\n\n-   [Read](/cpp/utility/from_chars)\n-   [View source](/index.php?title=cpp/utility/from_chars&action=edit \"This page is protected.\n    You can view its source [e]\")\n-   [View history](/index.php?title=cpp/utility/from_chars&action=history \"Past revisions of this page [h]\")\n\n##### Actions[](#)\n\n# std::from\\_chars\n\nFrom cppreference.com\n\n< [cpp](/cpp \"cpp\") | [utility](/cpp/utility \"cpp/utility\")\n\n[C++](/cpp \"cpp\")\n\n[Compiler support](/cpp/compiler_support \"cpp/compiler support\")\n\n[Freestanding and hosted](/cpp/freestanding \"cpp/freestanding\")\n\n[Language](/cpp/language \"cpp/language\")\n\n[Standard library](/cpp/standard_library \"cpp/standard library\")\n\n[Standard library headers](/cpp/header \"cpp/header\")\n\n[Named requirements](/cpp/named_req \"cpp/named req\")\n\n[Feature test macros](/cpp/feature_test \"cpp/feature test\") (C++20)\n\n[Language support library](/cpp/utility#Language_support \"cpp/utility\")\n\n[Concepts library](/cpp/concepts \"cpp/concepts\") (C++20)\n\n[Diagnostics library](/cpp/error \"cpp/error\")\n\n[Memory management library](/cpp/memory \"cpp/memory\")\n\n[Metaprogramming library](/cpp/meta \"cpp/meta\") (C++11)\n\n[General utilities library](/cpp/utility \"cpp/utility\")\n\n[Containers library](/cpp/container \"cpp/container\")\n\n[Iterators library](/cpp/iterator \"cpp/iterator\")\n\n[Ranges library](/cpp/ranges \"cpp/ranges\") (C++20)\n\n[Algorithms library](/cpp/algorithm \"cpp/algorithm\")\n\n[Strings library](/cpp/string \"cpp/string\")\n\n[Text processing library](/cpp/text \"cpp/text\")\n\n[Numerics library](/cpp/numeric \"cpp/numeric\")\n\n[Date and time library](/cpp/chrono \"cpp/chrono\")\n\n[Input/output library](/cpp/io \"cpp/io\")\n\n[Filesystem library](/cpp/filesystem \"cpp/filesystem\") (C++17)\n\n[Concurrency support library](/cpp/thread \"cpp/thread\") (C++11)\n\n[Execution control library](/cpp/execution \"cpp/execution\") (C++26)\n\n[Technical specifications](/cpp/experimental \"cpp/experimental\")\n\n[Symbols index](/cpp/symbol_index \"cpp/symbol index\")\n\n[External libraries](/cpp/links/libs \"cpp/links/libs\")\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:cpp/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n[Text processing library](/cpp/text \"cpp/text\")\n\n[Localization library](/cpp/locale \"cpp/locale\")\n\n[Regular expressions library](/cpp/regex \"cpp/regex\") (C++11)\n\n[Formatting library](/cpp/utility/format \"cpp/utility/format\") (C++20)\n\n[Null-terminated sequence utilities](/cpp/text#Null-terminated_sequence_utilities \"cpp/text\")\n\n[Byte strings](/cpp/string/byte \"cpp/string/byte\")\n\n[Multibyte strings](/cpp/string/multibyte \"cpp/string/multibyte\")\n\n[Wide strings](/cpp/string/wide \"cpp/string/wide\")\n\n[Primitive numeric conversions](/cpp/text#Primitive_numeric_conversions \"cpp/text\")\n\n[to\\_chars](/cpp/utility/to_chars \"cpp/utility/to chars\")\n\n(C++17)\n\n[to\\_chars\\_result](/cpp/utility/to_chars_result \"cpp/utility/to chars result\")\n\n(C++17)\n\nfrom\\_chars\n\n(C++17)\n\n[from\\_chars\\_result](/cpp/utility/from_chars_result \"cpp/utility/from chars result\")\n\n(C++17)\n\n[chars\\_format](/cpp/utility/chars_format \"cpp/utility/chars format\")\n\n(C++17)\n\n[Text encoding identifications](/cpp/text#Text_encoding_identifications \"cpp/text\")\n\n[text\\_encoding](/cpp/text/text_encoding \"cpp/text/text encoding\")\n\n(C++26)\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:cpp/text/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\nDefined in header `[<charconv>](/cpp/header/charconv \"cpp/header/charconv\")`\n\nstd::from\\_chars\\_result\n    from\\_chars( const char\\* first, const char\\* last,\n                /\\* integer-type \\*/& value, int base \\= 10 );\n\n(1)\n\n(since C++17)  \n(constexpr since C++23)\n\nstd::from\\_chars\\_result\n    from\\_chars( const char\\* first, const char\\* last,\n                /\\* floating-point-type \\*/& value,\n                std::chars\\_format fmt \\= std::chars\\_format::general );\n\n(2)\n\n(since C++17)\n\nAnalyzes the character sequence `[``first``,` `last``)` for a pattern described below. If no characters match the pattern or if the value obtained by parsing the matched characters is not representable in the type of `value`, `value` is unmodified, otherwise the characters matching the pattern are interpreted as a text representation of an arithmetic value, which is stored in `value`.\n\n1) Integer parsers: Expects the pattern identical to the one used by [std::strtol](/cpp/string/byte/strtol \"cpp/string/byte/strtol\") in the default (\"C\") locale and the given non-zero numeric base, except that\n\n-   `\"0x\"` or `\"0X\"` prefixes are not recognized if `base` is 16\n-   only the minus sign is recognized (not the plus sign), and only for signed integer types of `value`\n-   leading whitespace is not ignored.\n\nThe library provides overloads for all cv-unqualified(since C++23) signed and unsigned integer types and `char` as the referenced type of the parameter `value`.\n\n2) Floating-point parsers: Expects the pattern identical to the one used by [std::strtod](/cpp/string/byte/strtof \"cpp/string/byte/strtof\") in the default (\"C\") locale, except that\n\n-   the plus sign is not recognized outside of the exponent (only the minus sign is permitted at the beginning)\n-   if `fmt` has [std::chars\\_format::scientific](/cpp/utility/chars_format \"cpp/utility/chars format\") set but not [std::chars\\_format::fixed](/cpp/utility/chars_format \"cpp/utility/chars format\"), the exponent part is required (otherwise it is optional)\n-   if `fmt` has [std::chars\\_format::fixed](/cpp/utility/chars_format \"cpp/utility/chars format\") set but not [std::chars\\_format::scientific](/cpp/utility/chars_format \"cpp/utility/chars format\"), the optional exponent is not permitted\n-   if `fmt` is [std::chars\\_format::hex](/cpp/utility/chars_format \"cpp/utility/chars format\"), the prefix `\"0x\"` or `\"0X\"` is not permitted (the string `\"0x123\"` parses as the value `\"0\"` with unparsed remainder `\"x123\"`)\n-   leading whitespace is not ignored.\n\nIn any case, the resulting value is one of at most two floating-point values closest to the value of the string matching the pattern, after rounding according to [std::round\\_to\\_nearest](/cpp/types/numeric_limits/float_round_style \"cpp/types/numeric limits/float round style\").\n\nThe library provides overloads for all cv-unqualified standard(until C++23) floating-point types as the referenced type of the parameter `value`.\n\n## Contents\n\n-   [1 Parameters](#Parameters)\n-   [2 Return value](#Return_value)\n-   [3 Exceptions](#Exceptions)\n-   [4 Notes](#Notes)\n-   [5 Example](#Example)\n-   [6 Defect reports](#Defect_reports)\n-   [7 See also](#See_also)\n\n### Parameters\n\nfirst, last\n\n\\-\n\nvalid character range to parse\n\nvalue\n\n\\-\n\nthe out-parameter where the parsed value is stored if successful\n\nbase\n\n\\-\n\ninteger base to use: a value between 2 and 36 (inclusive).\n\nfmt\n\n\\-\n\nfloating-point formatting to use, a bitmask of type [std::chars\\_format](/cpp/utility/chars_format \"cpp/utility/chars format\")\n\n### Return value\n\nOn success, returns a value of type [std::from\\_chars\\_result](/cpp/utility/from_chars_result \"cpp/utility/from chars result\") such that `ptr` points at the first character not matching the pattern, or has the value equal to `last` if all characters match and `ec` is value-initialized.\n\nIf there is no pattern match, returns a value of type [std::from\\_chars\\_result](/cpp/utility/from_chars_result \"cpp/utility/from chars result\") such that `ptr` equals `first` and `ec` equals [std::errc::invalid\\_argument](/cpp/error/errc \"cpp/error/errc\"). `value` is unmodified.\n\nIf the pattern was matched, but the parsed value is not in the range representable by the type of `value`, returns value of type [std::from\\_chars\\_result](/cpp/utility/from_chars_result \"cpp/utility/from chars result\") such that `ec` equals [std::errc::result\\_out\\_of\\_range](/cpp/error/errc \"cpp/error/errc\") and `ptr` points at the first character not matching the pattern. `value` is unmodified.\n\n### Exceptions\n\nThrows nothing.\n\n### Notes\n\nUnlike other parsing functions in C++ and C libraries, `std::from_chars` is locale-independent, non-allocating, and non-throwing. Only a small subset of parsing policies used by other libraries (such as [std::sscanf](/cpp/io/c/fscanf \"cpp/io/c/fscanf\")) is provided. This is intended to allow the fastest possible implementation that is useful in common high-throughput contexts such as text-based interchange ([JSON](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JSON \"enwiki:JSON\") or [XML](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XML \"enwiki:XML\")).\n\nThe guarantee that `std::from_chars` can recover every floating-point value formatted by [std::to\\_chars](/cpp/utility/to_chars \"cpp/utility/to chars\") exactly is only provided if both functions are from the same implementation.\n\nA pattern consisting of a sign with no digits following it is treated as pattern that did not match anything.\n\n[Feature-test](/cpp/utility/feature_test \"cpp/utility/feature test\") macro\n\nValue\n\nStd\n\nFeature\n\n[`__cpp_lib_to_chars`](/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_to_chars \"cpp/feature test\")\n\n[`201611L`](/cpp/compiler_support/17#cpp_lib_to_chars_201611L \"cpp/compiler support/17\")\n\n(C++17)\n\nElementary string conversions (`std::from_chars`, [std::to\\_chars](/cpp/utility/to_chars \"cpp/utility/to chars\"))\n\n[`202306L`](/cpp/compiler_support/26#cpp_lib_to_chars_202306L \"cpp/compiler support/26\")\n\n(C++26)\n\nTesting for success or failure of [<charconv>](/cpp/header/charconv \"cpp/header/charconv\") functions\n\n[`__cpp_lib_constexpr_charconv`](/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_constexpr_charconv \"cpp/feature test\")\n\n[`202207L`](/cpp/compiler_support/23#cpp_lib_constexpr_charconv_202207L \"cpp/compiler support/23\")\n\n(C++23)\n\nAdd `constexpr` modifiers to `std::from_chars` and [std::to\\_chars](/cpp/utility/to_chars \"cpp/utility/to chars\") overloads for integral types\n\n### Example\n\nRun this code\n\n#include <cassert>\n#include <charconv>\n#include <iomanip>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <optional>\n#include <string\\_view>\n#include <system\\_error>\n\nint main()\n{\n    for (std::string\\_view const str : {\"1234\", \"15 foo\", \"bar\", \" 42\", \"5000000000\"})\n    {\n        std::cout << \"String: \" << std::quoted(str) << \". \";\n        int result{};\n        auto \\[ptr, ec\\] \\= std::from\\_chars(str.data(), str.data() + str.size(), result);\n\n        if (ec \\== std::errc())\n            std::cout << \"Result: \" << result << \", ptr -> \" << std::quoted(ptr) << '\\\\n';\n        else if (ec \\== std::errc::invalid\\_argument)\n            std::cout << \"This is not a number.\\\\n\";\n        else if (ec \\== std::errc::result\\_out\\_of\\_range)\n            std::cout << \"This number is larger than an int.\\\\n\";\n    }\n\n    // C++23's constexpr from\\_char demo / C++26's operator bool() demo:\n    auto to\\_int \\= \\[\\](std::string\\_view s) \\-> std::optional<int\\>\n    {\n        int value{};\n#if \\_\\_cpp\\_lib\\_to\\_chars >= 202306L\n        if (std::from\\_chars(s.data(), s.data() + s.size(), value))\n#else\n        if (std::from\\_chars(s.data(), s.data() + s.size(), value).ec \\== std::errc{})\n#endif\n            return value;\n        else\n            return std::nullopt;\n    };\n\n    assert(to\\_int(\"42\") \\== 42);\n    assert(to\\_int(\"foo\") \\== std::nullopt);\n#if \\_\\_cpp\\_lib\\_constexpr\\_charconv and \\_\\_cpp\\_lib\\_optional >= 202106\n    static\\_assert(to\\_int(\"42\") \\== 42);\n    static\\_assert(to\\_int(\"foo\") \\== std::nullopt);\n#endif\n}\n\nOutput:\n\nString: \"1234\". Result: 1234, ptr -> \"\"\nString: \"15 foo\". Result: 15, ptr -> \" foo\"\nString: \"bar\". This is not a number.\nString: \" 42\". This is not a number.\nString: \"5000000000\". This number is larger than an int.\n\n### Defect reports\n\nThe following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n\nDR\n\nApplied to\n\nBehavior as published\n\nCorrect behavior\n\n[LWG 2955](https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2955)\n\nC++17\n\nthis function was in [<utility>](/cpp/header/utility \"cpp/header/utility\") and used [std::error\\_code](/cpp/error/error_code \"cpp/error/error code\")\n\nmoved to [<charconv>](/cpp/header/charconv \"cpp/header/charconv\") and uses [std::errc](/cpp/error/errc \"cpp/error/errc\")\n\n[LWG 3373](https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3373)\n\nC++17\n\n`std::from_chars_result` might have additional members\n\nadditional members are prohibited\n\n### See also\n\n[from\\_chars\\_result](/cpp/utility/from_chars_result \"cpp/utility/from chars result\")\n\n(C++17)\n\nthe return type of std::from\\_chars  \n(class) [\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/dsc_from_chars_result&action=edit)\n\n[to\\_chars](/cpp/utility/to_chars \"cpp/utility/to chars\")\n\n(C++17)\n\nconverts an integer or floating-point value to a character sequence  \n(function) [\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/dsc_to_chars&action=edit)\n\n[stoistolstoll](/cpp/string/basic_string/stol \"cpp/string/basic string/stol\")\n\n(C++11)(C++11)(C++11)\n\nconverts a string to a signed integer  \n(function) [\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:cpp/string/basic_string/dsc_stol&action=edit)\n\n[stofstodstold](/cpp/string/basic_string/stof \"cpp/string/basic string/stof\")\n\n(C++11)(C++11)(C++11)\n\nconverts a string to a floating point value  \n(function) [\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:cpp/string/basic_string/dsc_stof&action=edit)\n\n[strtolstrtoll](/cpp/string/byte/strtol \"cpp/string/byte/strtol\")\n\n(C++11)\n\nconverts a byte string to an integer value  \n(function) [\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:cpp/string/byte/dsc_strtol&action=edit)\n\n[strtofstrtodstrtold](/cpp/string/byte/strtof \"cpp/string/byte/strtof\")\n\nconverts a byte string to a floating-point value  \n(function) [\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:cpp/string/byte/dsc_strtof&action=edit)\n\n[scanffscanfsscanf](/cpp/io/c/fscanf \"cpp/io/c/fscanf\")\n\nreads formatted input from [stdin](/cpp/io/c/std_streams \"cpp/io/c/std streams\"), a file stream or a buffer  \n(function) [\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:cpp/io/c/dsc_fscanf&action=edit)\n\n[operator>>](/cpp/io/basic_istream/operator_gtgt \"cpp/io/basic istream/operator gtgt\")\n\nextracts formatted data  \n(public member function of `std::basic_istream<CharT,Traits>`) [\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:cpp/io/basic_istream/dsc_operator_gtgt&action=edit)\n\n[Categories](/Special:Categories \"Special:Categories\"):\n\n-   [Pages using deprecated source tags](/index.php?title=Category:Pages_using_deprecated_source_tags&action=edit&redlink=1 \"Category:Pages using deprecated source tags (page does not exist)\")\n-   [Pages using deprecated enclose attributes](/index.php?title=Category:Pages_using_deprecated_enclose_attributes&action=edit&redlink=1 \"Category:Pages using deprecated enclose attributes (page does not exist)\")\n\n##### Navigation\n\n-   [Support us](http://www.cppreference.com/support)\n-   [Recent changes](/Special:RecentChanges \"A list of recent changes in the wiki [r]\")\n-   [FAQ](/Cppreference:FAQ)\n-   [Offline version](/Cppreference:Archives)\n\n##### Tools[](#)\n\n-   [What links here](/Special:WhatLinksHere/cpp/utility/from_chars \"A list of all wiki pages that link here [j]\")\n-   [Related changes](/Special:RecentChangesLinked/cpp/utility/from_chars \"Recent changes in pages linked from this page [k]\")\n-   [Upload file](http://upload.cppreference.com/w/Special:Upload \"Upload files [u]\")\n-   [Special pages](/Special:SpecialPages \"A list of all special pages [q]\")\n-   [Printable version](javascript:print\\(\\); \"Printable version of this page [p]\")\n-   [Permanent link](/index.php?title=cpp/utility/from_chars&oldid=179101 \"Permanent link to this revision of this page\")\n-   [Page information](/index.php?title=cpp/utility/from_chars&action=info \"More information about this page\")\n\n-   In other languages\n\n-   [Deutsch](https://de.cppreference.com/cpp/utility/from_chars \"cpp/utility/from chars – Deutsch\")\n-   [Español](http://es.cppreference.com/cpp/utility/from_chars \"cpp/utility/from chars – español\")\n-   [Français](http://fr.cppreference.com/cpp/utility/from_chars \"cpp/utility/from chars – français\")\n-   [Italiano](http://it.cppreference.com/cpp/utility/from_chars \"cpp/utility/from chars – italiano\")\n-   [日本語](http://ja.cppreference.com/cpp/utility/from_chars \"cpp/utility/from chars – 日本語\")\n-   [Português](http://pt.cppreference.com/cpp/utility/from_chars \"cpp/utility/from chars – português\")\n-   [Русский](http://ru.cppreference.com/cpp/utility/from_chars \"cpp/utility/from chars – русский\")\n-   [中文](http://zh.cppreference.com/cpp/utility/from_chars \"cpp/utility/from chars – 中文\")",
